From 4e0f4b3b5aeedc74338c06e3e6b1896b15b73fc6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 06:29:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] provider, gui: a listing's budgets add up, and one provider's
 fetch models no longer re-lists past them (#4065)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

What changed

The budgets a listing of the plugins' providers is made of added up past
the budgets its callers set: the host let one provider spend listWait
(20s) on its models hook plus the wait for a due renewal (RENEW_WAIT,
15s) before it, and a provider with two accounts spent them back to
back. One provider could be allowed 35s (40s with a second account) —
past the 30s refreshDeadline the background refresh asks under and past
the editor's own 20s — so pressing Fetch models, or a refresh, died with
a bare "context deadline exceeded" while no vendor had failed: every
provider is asked side by side, and the sum of the budgets was the only
thing over.

Now the host's own bounds hold by construction:

- host.js info(): the wait for a due renewal (fresh) spends the models
  hook's own budget — the hook is given what is left of listWait, and
  the renewal wait can no longer be added on top of it.
- host.js providers(): a provider's accounts are listed side by side
  (the first no longer waited for before the rest), so one provider
  costs one listWait, not one per account.
- gui/providers.go, case "models": the editor's budget is 30s, the same
  the host bounds one providers RPC with, instead of 20s — shorter than
  even one provider's worst case under the old arithmetic.

A provider whose renewal is slow then lists late (its hook given up on
alone, said so in listError as any other stuck listing) instead of
taking the whole listing past the caller's deadline (#4065).

Run

- TestProviderListCoversAccountsSideBySide, two accounts whose hooks
  each take 1.5s under a 2.5s caller budget: with the product files at
  the base (68b31ce23) and the tests kept, the listing dies with
  "context deadline exceeded"; with the fix it stands and both accounts
  are listed (1.6s).
- TestRenewalWaitSpendsTheListBudget, a renewal that never finishes
  waited 15s before a 5s hook given 6s of its own, under a 17s
  refreshDeadline: with the product files at the base the listing goes
  past refreshDeadline and nothing is kept; with the fix the listing
  stands and the provider fell back, its listError saying so.
- internal/plugin full suite (go test ./internal/plugin -tags nogui):
  ok, and gofmt/vet clean.

